  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001, rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000) yielded a low accuracy of ~48.5%, giving us a weak baseline with no information about whether image features carry useful signal. The most critical uncertainty at this stage is whether the image modality is informative at all, since it determines whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_001: it changes only the modality while keeping profile setting (single) and encoder complexity comparable. If image_only substantially outperforms the RNA baseline, it signals that image features are the stronger signal and multimodal configs become high-priority. If it performs similarly or worse, we can focus remaining budget on RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. With 8 experiments left, resolving this fundamental modality question early prevents wasting budget on multimodal configurations that may not help."
}

